{
  "tema": 7482,
  "slug": "animar-animarse",
  "titulo": "Animar vs animarse",
  "subtitulo": "Animó la fiesta. Anímate, ven con nosotros.",
  "foto": "t09.jpg",
  "regla": "Animar algo = to liven up. Animar a alguien = to cheer someone up. Animar a alguien a + infinitive = to encourage someone to. Animarse = to cheer up, or to decide to do something: ¿Te animas a venir? = Are you up for coming?",
  "comparada_kwiziq": "2026-10-10",
  "secciones": [
    {
      "id": "regla",
      "titulo": "The rule",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "usos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "forma": "animar algo",
              "texto": "_to liven up_: **la música animó la fiesta**."
            },
            {
              "forma": "animar a alguien",
              "texto": "_to cheer someone up_: **anímala, está triste**."
            },
            {
              "forma": "animar a alguien a + infinitive",
              "texto": "_to encourage someone to_: **me animó a estudiar**. Two **a**'s."
            },
            {
              "forma": "animarse",
              "texto": "_to cheer up_: **¡anímate!**"
            },
            {
              "forma": "animarse a + infinitive",
              "texto": "_to feel up for, decide to_: **¿te animas a venir?**, **no me animo a decirle**."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "**¿Te animas?** is a super common Mexican invitation: _Are you in?_"
        },
        {
          "tipo": "texto",
          "texto": "Tip: **animar** puts energy into something; **animarse** finds the energy inside you."
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "ejemplos",
      "titulo": "Examples",
      "bloques": [
        {
          "tipo": "ejemplos",
          "lista": [
            {
              "es": "La llegada de las chavas ==animó== la fiesta.",
              "en": "The girls arriving livened up the party."
            },
            {
              "es": "La música de banda ==animaba== mucho el ambiente.",
              "en": "The banda music really livened up the atmosphere."
            },
            {
              "es": "Clara está triste. Ve y ==anímala==.",
              "en": "Clara's sad. Go cheer her up."
            },
            {
              "es": "Julián me ==animó a== inscribirme en el maratón.",
              "en": "Julián encouraged me to sign up for the marathon."
            },
            {
              "es": "¡==Anímate==! Ya va a pasar.",
              "en": "Cheer up! It'll pass."
            },
            {
              "es": "Vamos a ir a la playa. ¿==Te animas==?",
              "en": "We're going to the beach. You in?"
            },
            {
              "es": "No ==me animo a== decirle la verdad.",
              "en": "I can't bring myself to tell her the truth."
            }
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
